  <Document>
    <name>Expedition 51 — 941 Categorized &amp; Color-Coded POIs</name>
    <Folder><name>ATTRACTION (69)</name>
      <Placemark><name>Carillon Canal National Historic Lock</name><description>[Day 1] Historic 19th-century military canal on the Ottawa River built after the War of 1812 with a massive 20-metre single hydraulic guillotine lock.</description><Point><coordinates>-74.376,45.568,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Manic-5 (Daniel-Johnson Dam)</name><description>[Day 3] World's largest multiple-arch hollow buttress dam. 214 m high, 1.3 km wide. Marvel of modern engineering.</description><Point><coordinates>-68.7247,50.6406,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Gagnon Ghost Town (Abandoned Boreal Streets)</name><description>[Day 3] Km 485 on QC-389. Thriving 1970s mining city demolished in 1985. Concrete sidewalks and street curbs still intact in the forest.</description><Point><coordinates>-68.1667,51.9167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Fermont Windbreak Wall ('Le Mur')</name><description>[Day 3] Famous 1.3 km long, 5-story windbreak building sheltering the subarctic mining community from freezing arctic gales.</description><Point><coordinates>-67.0833,52.7917,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>The Truck — Giant Terex Mining Dump Truck Display</name><description>[Day 3] Colossal retired open-pit iron ore haul truck on display in Labrador City — classic motorcycle scale photo-op!</description><Point><coordinates>-66.900059,52.95079,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Churchill Falls Underground Hydro Plant</name><description>[Day 4] 5,428 MW underground power station hollowed out of solid Precambrian granite 305 m beneath the surface.</description><Point><coordinates>-64.0,53.5333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>L'Anse Amour 7,500-Year Burial Mound</name><description>[Day 5] The oldest known human-constructed funeral burial mound in North America (Maritime Archaic Indigenous culture, 5500 BCE), marked by a stone cairn.</description><Point><coordinates>-56.865,51.465,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>HMS Raleigh 1922 Shipwreck &amp; Raleigh Trail</name><description>[Day 5] Remains of the 600-ft British Royal Navy heavy cruiser HMS Raleigh that ran aground in blinding fog in 1922 beneath Point Amour. Steam boilers visible on beach.</description><Point><coordinates>-56.868,51.455,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Red Bay Basque Whaling Station (UNESCO)</name><description>[Day 5] UNESCO World Heritage Site. 16th-century Basque whaling headquarters in North America. Sunken galleons &amp; tryworks rendering ovens.</description><Point><coordinates>-56.4167,51.7333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>L'Anse aux Meadows (UNESCO Viking Settlement)</name><description>[Day 6] Only confirmed Norse Viking site in North America (circa 1000 AD). Authentic turf houses, blacksmith shop, and archaeological museum.</description><Point><coordinates>-55.5314,51.5956,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Grenfell Historic Properties &amp; Museum (St. Anthony)</name><description>[Day 6] Historic mission headquarters of Dr. Wilfred Grenfell who brought modern medicine to remote Newfoundland and Labrador. Historic home and museum.</description><Point><coordinates>-55.599,51.363,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Grenfell Historic Properties (St. Anthony)</name><description>[Day 6] Museum, historic home, and interpretive centre honoring medical missionary Sir Wilfred Grenfell in St. Anthony.</description><Point><coordinates>-55.5845,51.3642,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Norstead Viking Village &amp; Snorri Knarr Ship</name><description>[Day 7] Living history Viking trading port featuring the 54-foot replica knarr merchant ship 'Snorri', axe throwing, and forge.</description><Point><coordinates>-55.52,51.599,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Broom Point Traditional Cod Fishing Premises</name><description>[Day 8] Preserved 1960s inshore cod-fishing family cabin and workshop in Gros Morne. Restored wooden dories, drying flakes, and living history.</description><Point><coordinates>-57.872,49.831,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Wreckhouse Extreme Winds Corridor</name><description>[Day 10] Legendary coastal funnel where southeastern mountain gusts exceed 200 km/h, famously blowing trains off their tracks.</description><Point><coordinates>-59.325,47.715,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>The Gaelic College / Colaisde na Gàidhlig (St. Ann's)</name><description>[Day 11] Historic Gaelic cultural learning institution founded in 1938 at the start of the Cabot Trail in St. Ann's; preserves Highland Scottish heritage and Celtic arts.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.5985,46.273,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Anne of Green Gables Heritage Place</name><description>[Day 13] Historic 19th-century Victorian farmstead, Haunted Wood trail, and Lovers Lane that inspired L.M. Montgomery's classic novel.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.385,46.4917,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>L.M. Montgomery's Birthplace (New London)</name><description>[Day 13] Cozy white-and-green farmhouse in New London where author Lucy Maud Montgomery was born in 1874. Displays replica wedding dress and scrapbooks.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.468,46.505,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Anne of Green Gables Museum at Silver Bush</name><description>[Day 13] Historic Campbell family homestead where Montgomery was married. Features Matthew's carriage rides and views over the Lake of Shining Waters.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.535,46.521,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Lake of Shining Waters (Park Corner)</name><description>[Day 13] Pristine freshwater pond glistening behind the coastal barrier dunes immortalized by Montgomery as 'The Lake of Shining Waters'.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.538,46.525,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>French River Overlook &amp; Fishing Cove</name><description>[Day 13] Postcard-perfect PEI landscape of rolling emerald green potato fields sloping down to colorful fishing shacks on the quiet river inlet.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.513,46.516,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Cavendish Beach Sandstone Sea Stacks</name><description>[Day 13] Towering red sandstone arches, caves, and barrier dunes glowing fiery red in the late afternoon sun along the Cavendish coastline.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.415,46.498,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Site of L.M. Montgomery's Cavendish Home</name><description>[Day 13] Peaceful wooded homestead where Montgomery was raised by her grandparents and wrote Anne of Green Gables. Path through apple orchard.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.382,46.486,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>St. Dunstan's Basilica (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Magnificent French Gothic twin-spired stone basilica and National Historic Site in downtown Charlottetown.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.1258,46.2332,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Victoria Row (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Pedestrian-only cobblestone Victorian street lined with red-brick cafés, patios, boutiques, and live music next to Confederation Centre.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.1272,46.2345,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Anne of Green Gables Museum (Park Corner / Silver Bush)</name><description>[Day 14] Historic 1872 Campbell homestead at Park Corner overlooking the 'Lake of Shining Waters' where L.M. Montgomery was married.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.5512,46.5192,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Avonlea Village (Cavendish, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Turn-of-the-century heritage village in Cavendish featuring historic schoolhouse, church, and local PEI artisan food stalls.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.3835,46.4898,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>The Bottle Houses (Cap-Egmont, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Whimsical folk-art village of three shimmering buildings and gardens constructed from over 25,000 recycled glass bottles.</description><Point><coordinates>-64.1285,46.4012,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Canadian Potato Museum (O'Leary, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Home of the world's largest potato sculpture, heritage farm machinery hall, and PEI Potato Country Kitchen.</description><Point><coordinates>-64.2285,46.7058,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Acadian Museum of PEI (Miscouche, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Chronicles over 300 years of Island Acadian history and culture in Miscouche near Summerside.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.8615,46.4312,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Prince Edward Island Regiment Museum (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Military museum housed at Queen Charlotte Armoury showcasing PEI's regimental history from 1875 to present.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.1212,46.2385,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Village musical acadien (Abram-Village, PEI)</name><description>[Day 14] Lively Acadian cultural and musical centre in the Évangéline region featuring fiddle music, step-dancing, bakery, and crêperie.</description><Point><coordinates>-64.0725,46.4518,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Saint John City Market (1876)</name><description>[Day 15] Canada's oldest continuously operating farmer's market, featuring a unique timber roof hand-crafted by 19th-century shipbuilders shaped like an inverted ship's hull.</description><Point><coordinates>-66.0633,45.2733,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Hartland World's Longest Covered Bridge (1901)</name><description>[Day 15] The longest covered wooden bridge in the world (391 m), built in 1901 across the Saint John River. You can ride your bikes right through!</description><Point><coordinates>-67.528,46.297,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Saint John Firefighters' Museum (Saint John, NB)</name><description>[Day 16] Historic No. 2 Engine House museum in Uptown Saint John displaying antique steam pumpers and Great Fire of 1877 artifacts.</description><Point><coordinates>-66.0568,45.2742,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Carleton Martello Tower National Historic Site (Saint John, NB)</name><description>[Day 16] 1812 circular stone coastal fortification with WWII fire-control superstructure offering 360-degree views over Saint John Harbour and the Bay of Fundy.</description><Point><coordinates>-66.0762,45.2528,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>AREA 506 Waterfront Container Village (Saint John, NB)</name><description>[Day 16] Vibrant colourful shipping-container village on the Saint John waterfront featuring local vendors, murals, food trucks, and waterfront stage.</description><Point><coordinates>-66.0628,45.2682,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Broom Point Harbour Historic Fishing Premises</name><description>[Day 8] Restored 19th-century Mudge family fishing premises &amp; dory house on the rocky coast of Gros Morne National Park.</description><Point><coordinates>-57.868433,49.83712,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Whale Interpretive Centre (Pleasant Bay)</name><description>[Day 12] Marine museum in Pleasant Bay dedicated to pilot, fin, and humpback whales of the Gulf of St. Lawrence.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.798463,46.832386,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Cape Smokey Gondola (38696 Cabot Trail)</name><description>[Day 11] 8-passenger alpine gondola rising 320m from the Atlantic Ocean to the summit of Cape Smokey.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.422235,46.628343,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
