    <Folder><name>HIKE (29)</name>
      <Placemark><name>Port-au-Persil Waterfall &amp; Historic Chapel</name><description>[Day 2] Hidden Charlevoix cove off Route 138 where a fresh mountain waterfall cascades directly over granite rocks into the saltwater St. Lawrence estuary.</description><Point><coordinates>-69.887,47.8045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Crystal Falls Hiking Trail (Labrador City)</name><description>[Day 3] Scenic short hike overlooking cascading Crystal Falls between the Labrador border and Labrador City.</description><Point><coordinates>-66.973953,52.94501,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Harrie Lake Trail (Labrador West)</name><description>[Day 3] Peaceful boreal lakeside walking trail near Labrador City and Wabush.</description><Point><coordinates>-66.935664,52.933453,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Jean Lake Walking Trail (Wabush)</name><description>[Day 3] 5.5 km groomed boardwalk and gravel walking trail looping around Jean Lake between Wabush and Labrador City.</description><Point><coordinates>-66.881416,52.898039,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Tracey Hill 700-Step Overlook (Red Bay)</name><description>[Day 5] 700 wooden boardwalk stairs climbing Tracey Hill behind the Red Bay UNESCO Basque Whaling Station. Panoramic view over Saddle Island icebergs.</description><Point><coordinates>-56.425,51.733,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Burnt Cape Ecological Reserve (Arctic Barrens)</name><description>[Day 6] Alien subarctic landscape near Raleigh resembling the surface of Mars. Coastal limestone sea arches, wave-carved caves, and rare arctic plants.</description><Point><coordinates>-55.76,51.605,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Green Point Geological Golden Spike (GSSP)</name><description>[Day 8] UN Global Boundary Stratotype Section and Point (GSSP). Layered coastal shale cliffs marking 500-million-year-old geological boundary with graptolite fossils.</description><Point><coordinates>-57.962,49.682,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Trout River Eastern Point Clifftop Trail</name><description>[Day 8] Spectacular 30-minute wooden stairway trail rising to open grassy cliff headlands where sheep graze above crashing Gulf swells.</description><Point><coordinates>-58.125,49.493,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Corner Brook Stream Trail</name><description>[Day 9] Lush gorge boardwalk, waterfalls, and salmon stream trail winding right through the heart of Corner Brook.</description><Point><coordinates>-57.9432,48.9488,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>White Point Unknown Sailor Clifftop Trail</name><description>[Day 11] Rugged coastal path out onto an isolated rocky headland jutting into the Atlantic. Sea bird colonies and the solitary white cross of the Unknown Sailor's grave.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.355,46.903,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Black Brook Cove Waterfall &amp; Ocean Beach</name><description>[Day 11] Spectacular Atlantic ocean beach in Cape Breton Highlands where a freshwater mountain brook and waterfall cascade over sea cliffs onto the sand.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.331,46.777,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Skyline Trail Boardwalk Hike</name><description>[Day 12] World-famous 2-hour coastal hike to a dramatic wooden boardwalk looking down on the Cabot Trail hairpins, crashing ocean, and grazing moose.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.875,46.745,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Dickson Falls Lush Mossy Gorge Boardwalk</name><description>[Day 14] Fundy National Park's most popular short hike: a 1.5 km wooden boardwalk descending into a cool, lush microclimate ravine blanketed in moss and ferns.</description><Point><coordinates>-64.962,45.589,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Eau Claire Gorges Conservation Area</name><description>[Day 18] Dramatic 2.5 km Canadian Shield trail through an ancient granite river gorge near Mattawa with a 40-foot waterfall and 1870s logger cabin ruins.</description><Point><coordinates>-78.915,46.262,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Southhead Lighthouse Trail Parking</name><description>[Day 10] Trailhead parking at Bottle Cove for the coastal hike out to Southhead Lighthouse at the mouth of the Bay of Islands.</description><Point><coordinates>-58.406115,49.117561,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Bottle Cove Coastal Hiking Trail</name><description>[Day 10] Scenic coastal headland boardwalk and cliff trail overlooking turquoise coves.</description><Point><coordinates>-58.41103,49.11682,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Barachois Pond Provincial Park — Erin Mountain Trailhead</name><description>[Day 10] Trailhead to the 340m summit of Erin Mountain overlooking Barachois Pond and the Long Range Mountains.</description><Point><coordinates>-58.261689,48.481289,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>James Cook Heritage Trail (Lark Harbour)</name><description>[Day 10] Coastal heritage trail commemorating Captain James Cook's 1767 hydrographic survey of the Bay of Islands.</description><Point><coordinates>-58.363617,49.090538,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>The Lone Shieling (Grande Anse Old-Growth Forest)</name><description>[Day 12] Stone Scottish crofter's hut replica nestled inside a 350-year-old sugar maple forest loop trail.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.720546,46.813186,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Mica Hill Trailhead (Cape Breton Highlands)</name><description>[Day 12] Barrens and sparkling mica rock outcrop hike along the northern Cabot Trail.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.423856,46.851964,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Jack Pine Trailhead (Cabot Trail)</name><description>[Day 11] Coastal cliff loop through windswept jack pine stands and pink granite ledges.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.332024,46.779965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Green Cove Trailhead (Cabot Trail)</name><description>[Day 11] Short 200m granite boardwalk out to the Atlantic surf at Green Cove.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.32499,46.751525,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Acadian Trailhead (Cape Breton Highlands NP)</name><description>[Day 12] Panoramic ridge trail climbing above the Chéticamp River valley and Acadian coast.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.949821,46.647263,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Camel's Back Trail (St. Lunaire-Griquet)</name><description>[Day 7] Scenic coastal ridge hike overlooking St. Lunaire Bay and the northern ocean.</description><Point><coordinates>-55.449084,51.535631,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Cape Onion &amp; Raleigh Trailhead (NL A0K 4J0)</name><description>[Day 7] Volcanic pillow lava cliffs, fossils, and iceberg lookout trails at the tip of Cape Onion.</description><Point><coordinates>-55.642,51.6115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Pejepscot Lookout Trailhead (Fundy Trail Parkway)</name><description>[Day 15] Short coastal trail to the Pejepscot cliff overlook.</description><Point><coordinates>-65.429,45.4095,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Bradshaw Lookout Trailhead (Fundy Trail Parkway)</name><description>[Day 15] Trailhead to Bradshaw Lookout overlooking 250m coastal cliffs.</description><Point><coordinates>-65.460733,45.39887,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Melvin Beach Trail (Fundy Trail Parkway)</name><description>[Day 15] Coastal trail descending toward Melvin Beach and Pangburn cliffs.</description><Point><coordinates>-65.4545,45.3945,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Grand Falls Gorge Trail (Malabeam Promenade)</name><description>[Day 15] Cliffside boardwalk and suspension bridge trail overlooking the roaring 23m cataract of Grand Falls.</description><Point><coordinates>-67.7395,47.0495,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
