      <Placemark><name>Green Point Campground (Gros Morne NP)</name><description>[Day 9] World-class coastal drive-in campground in Gros Morne perched on seaside bluffs overlooking the Gulf of St. Lawrence. Ocean sunset, campfire surf.</description><Point><coordinates>-57.85,49.6833,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Marine Atlantic Overnight Ferry (Private 2-Berth Stateroom Cabin)</name><description>[Day 10] Private 2-berth en-suite stateroom aboard MV Highlanders / MV Blue Puttees. Boarding 21:45, sailing 23:45 across Cabot Strait to North Sydney arriving 07:00 AM.</description><Point><coordinates>-59.136,47.575,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Broad Cove Campground (Cape Breton Highlands NP)</name><description>[Day 11] Spectacular oceanfront National Park campground in Ingonish directly on the Cabot Trail. Sandy ocean beach, hot showers, flush toilets, campfire pits.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.4,46.68,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Chéticamp Campground (Cape Breton Highlands NP)</name><description>[Day 12] Tucked in the mountain valley at the western park entrance of the Cabot Trail. Hot showers, walking distance to Chéticamp village.</description><Point><coordinates>-60.98,46.64,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Cavendish Campground (Prince Edward Island National Park)</name><description>[Day 13] Pristine Parks Canada oceanfront campground directly on the Gulf of St. Lawrence red sand dunes and sandstone cliffs. Walking access to Cavendish Beach and 3 min to Anne of Green Gables.</description><Point><coordinates>-63.402,46.495,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Fundy National Park (Headquarters Campground)</name><description>[Day 14] Perched on seaside bluffs overlooking the Bay of Fundy above Alma harbor. Heated washrooms, hot showers, walk down to fresh Fundy lobster.</description><Point><coordinates>-64.952,45.598,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
